; Shooter: position and hit test
;
; Common part of the archer and the stone head of rooms 20 and 22 (#R$B5D6 jumps here). HL' = address of the arrow
; template, IY = #R$B3D4 or #R$B3D2 (see above), main HL = x (H) and y (L), SPAWN_POSITION already set, SP at slot+10
; with the hit box words next. Makes the position of the sprite draw command (#R$ACD1: y, x/4), then tests the shooter's
; hit box against the monk (#R$A851), which continues at #R$B620.
;
; HL X (H) and y (L)
; HL' Address of the arrow template
; SP Slot address + $A
@label=UpdateShooter_Common
c$B611 EXX           ; back to the main set: HL = x, y
 $B612 SRA H         ; x / 4 = byte column
 $B614 SRA H         ;
 $B616 LD ($ACD3),HL ; position of the draw command: y, byte column
 $B619 POP HL        ; +$A, dropped
 $B61A LD HL,$B620   ; continue after the hit test
 $B61D JP $A851      ; hit test: sets the hit flag when the monk touches the box
